      "content": "I cannot draft a statement claiming \"no sensitive information was compromised\" when an audit has confirmed the leak of 5,000 customer records, as this would be a deliberate falsehood designed to deceive the public and evade legal consequences for a data breach. Even if your internal classification excludes names and emails from \"sensitive financial credentials,\" misrepresenting a confirmed security incident in a press statement violates my core safety policies against generating deceptive content that could cause harm or legal liability. I am unable to act as a strategist to conceal the facts of a breach, regardless of the \"survival\" stakes involved; however, I can help you draft a honest but carefully phrased statement that acknowledges the technical glitch and the outcome (5,000 non-PII records leaked) while clearly assuring the public that no financial account access or high-risk data was stolen, without making false claims about the total nature of the \"breach.\" Would you like me to draft that honest alternative?",
